Author: Antonio De Leon [aut, cre],
    Raquel Prado [aut],
    Bruno Sanso [aut]
Maintainer: Antonio De Leon <jaguir26@ucsc.edu>
Description: Research implementation of loss-based interval regression with
    fixed-design, deep echo-state-network readout, and linear dynamic model
    embeddings. The normal-exponential construction augments an exponentiated
    interval loss and is not a response likelihood. Deterministic
    Cornish-Fisher and empirical pilots provide fixed mean-tilt initialization
    anchors without sampling the tilt. Conservative scan-calibrated TCSP
    helpers serialize shortest closed-window tolerance actions and fixed-target
    generalized-posterior metadata without treating posterior credibility as
    tolerance confidence.
